  "version": "2026-10-05.2",
  "about": "Known tags and consent banners. A pattern matches a request when its host ends with `host` (any host when absent), its path starts with `path`, and its path and query contain `contains`. `load` is the tag's script loading; `hit` is the tag sending data; `source` finds the tag in a page's HTML. A hit's event is the hit pattern's `event` when it has one, otherwise the value of the first of the vendor's `events` keys found in the query or in a line of the POST body. A consent banner's `accept` is the CSS selector of its accept-all button.",
